  "strategy": "1. **Approach and Rationale**\nA novel approach based on **pulse-shaped waveforms** is utilized to find a sparse representation of the function h(x). This method combines a truncation based on the determined critical frequency for zero-overlap and an optimization employing **diffusion-based regularization** to manage the formation's propagation characteristics. The approach:\n   - Uses harmonic analysis to determine the space-frequency characteristics essential for minimizing overlap\n   - Balances time-frequency domains through diffusion-based optimization\n   - Reduces the effective scope of combinatorial searches through a sparse representation\n   - Avoids local minima by incorporating frequency-domain regularization\n\n2. **Mathematical Specification**\nOur solution satisfies:\n   \\(h(x) \\in [0, 1]\\)\n   \\(\\int_0^2 h(x) dx = 1\\)\n\nDerivation:\n   Let \\( \\omega_{cr} = 2\\pi / L \\) where L is the critical wavelength determined from:\n      \\[ \\omega_{cr}^2 = \\frac{\\langle E \\rangle}{2\\pi\\epsilon_0} \\]\n   \n   where \\( \\langle E \\rangle \\) is the average energy density over the interval [0,2].\n\nIn discrete form with resolution n_points:\n   \\( h = [0,\\dots,0, w_1, \\dots, w_m, 0,\\dots,0] \\)\n\n   where:\n   \\( \\sum_{i} h[i] \\cdot dx = 1 \\)\n   \\( dx = 2/n_{points} \\)\n   \\( m \\ll n_{points} \\)\n\nObjective:\n   Minimize \\( C_5 = \\max_k \\int_0^2 h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx \\)\n\n3. **Implementation Procedure**\n   a. **Initialize Parameters**:\n      - Determine critical frequency using EDF computations\n      - Set \u03bb_0 = 2k_{max} (frequency domain filter)\n      - \u03bc = 0.1 (weight for diffusion penalty)\n\n   b. **Setup Evolutionary Parameters**:\n      - n_genes = ceil(n_points/2)\n      - Selection assortativity r = 0.7\n      - Mutation rate \u03b1 = 0.05\n\n   c. **Generate Initial Population**:\n        i. Create candidate pulses at random positions:\n            \\( h_0(x) = \\tanh(x - x_i / \\sigma) \\)\n        ii. Apply sparse projection with:\n            \\( \\sigma = \\frac{2\\pi}{k_{max}} \\)\n        iii. Project to satisfy integral constraint:\n            \\( h(x) = \\tanh(x) \\) rescaled\n\n   d. **Fitness Evaluation**:\n        i. Compute correlation matrix C:\n            \\( C_{i,j} = \\int_0^2 h_i(x)h_j(x+k)dx \\)\n        ii. Optimize error penalty term:\n            \\( \\mathcal{E} = \\mu C_{\\max} + (1-\\mu)\\|h\\|_{L^2}^2 \\)\n        iii. Floating-point gradient descent adjustment:\n\n   e. **Selection**:\n        Sort by fitness, select top 25% \n        Use tournament selection with size 6\n\n   f. **Crossover**:\n        Gaussian crossover method:\n            \\( p_crossover = 0.7 \\)\n            \\( child = p_b \\cdot parent_1 + (1-p_b) \\cdot parent_2 \\)\n\n   g. **Diffusion-Based Evolution**:\n        Apply diffusion matrix:\n            \\( D = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0.1 & 0.05 & ... & 0 \\end{bmatrix} \\)\n        Update rule:\n            \\( parent_{new} = Dparent_{old} + \\mu \\cdot g(t) \\)\n        where g(t) follows Bernoulli with p normally distributed\n\n   h. **Constraint Handling**:\n        Integral constraint enforced by:\n            \\( h_tproj = (h - \\bar{h}) \\times scale \\)\n        Boundary conditions:\n            \\( h_{\\min} = 0, h_{\\max} = 1 \\)\n        Smooth adjustment with function:\n            \\( f(x) = \\min(1, \\frac{dx}{dx_{max}}) \\)\n\n4. **Search Choices & Variations**\n   a. Core hyperparameters:\n        - Fingerprint decay coefficient \u03b2 = 1.25\n        - Threshold density \u03c1_crit = 0.6\n        - Smoothing parameter \u03c4 = 0.05\n\n   b. Adaptive strategies:\n        - Variable mutation rate: \u03b1 = 0.01 * \u03be(t)\n        - Pulse shape evolution (Brownian motion)\n        - Noise injection for diversity (\u03c3_n = 0.005)\n\n   c. When:\n        - Coordinate locks occur: \u226410 linear search steps\n        - Initial plateau detected (>5 generations)\n        - Correlation < 0.95 of theoretical minimum\n\n5. **Compute Budget & Robustness**\n   a. Dominant operations: correlation matrix computations of size n_genes \u00d7 n_genes\n   b. Memory: O(n_genes\u00b2) for intermediate storage\n   c. Schedule:\n        - Initial phase: 600f COE (Computational Operations Equivalent)\n        - Evolution phase: 500f COE\n        - Optimization phase: 200f COE\n   d. Time checkpoints:\n        - 800f: Validate diversity thresholds\n        - 1100f: Filter solutions by 95% robustness check\n        - 1250f: Restart kernel if stability metrics below threshold\n\n6. **Validation and Return Contract**\n   a. Feasibility checks:\n        - Integral sum must satisfy: |sum(h) - 120| < 20\n        - Boundary adherence: clip all values to [0,1]\n        - Floating-point stability: ensure all intermediates >1e-8\n   b. Re-evaluation protocol:\n        i. Compute correlation matrix\n        ii. Extract maximum eigenvalue\n        iii. Scale by dx factor\n        iv. Verify identity constraint holds to \u00b11%\n\n   c. Statistical checks:\n        Run comparative diffusion trials (n=3)\n        Verify by implementing:\n            \\( \\frac{\\partial \\mathcal{E}}{\\partial h} = 0 \\)\n\n   d. Final tuning:\n        Minimize \\( J = \\gamma C_5 + (1-\\gamma)D(h) \\)\n        with \u03b7 = 0.9 active learning rate\n        and selection threshold \u03c1_crit = 0.6\n\n   The algorithm iterates until computational budget expires, returning the solution with minimal verified C5.",
